Add `VectorKMeansConfig` (`vector_kmeans_config` on `ModuleKMeansPalettizerConfig`) to set the k-means++ candidates per seeding step (`n_local_trials`), restarts, iteration cap and convergence tolerance of vector palettization (`cluster_dim > 1`). Vector k-means now clusters on a CUDA GPU, with flash-kmeans when it is installed and a batched PyTorch loop otherwise or for sensitivity-weighted clustering, and on CPU with scikit-learn, falling back to the PyTorch loop with a warning when scikit-learn is not installed.
